📚 The doc issue
Currently the docs show the following:
torch::nn::Linear model(3, 4);
torch::load(model, "model.pt");

torch::optim::SGD sgd(/*lr=*&zwj;/0.9);
std::istringstream stream("...");
torch::load(sgd, stream);

auto tensor = torch::ones({3, 4});
torch::load(tensor, "my_tensor.pt");
The comments that start with sgd(/* is never closed. This is probably not intentional.
Suggest a potential alternative/fix
The following snippet can be used instead
torch::nn::Linear model(3, 4);
torch::load(model, "model.pt");

torch::optim::SGD sgd(/*lr=*/0.9);
std::istringstream stream("...");
torch::load(sgd, stream);

auto tensor = torch::ones({3, 4});
torch::load(tensor, "my_tensor.pt");
cc @svekars @carljparker @jbschlosser

Today, if you use torch._foreach_copy_(dsts, srcs) where dsts are in one dtype and srcs are in another, the foreach copy takes the slow path and does not batch any of the copies:



      pytorch/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/ForeachBinaryOpList.cu


        Lines 265 to 269
      in
      e06bff8







           if (!can_use_fast_route( 




                   self, src, /* does_op_promote_integer_inputs_to_float */ false)) { 




             return at::native::foreach_tensor_copy_list_kernel_slow_( 




                 self, src, non_blocking); 




           } 





The feature request is for the copies to be batched so that the copying achieves better GPU bandwidth and has lower CPU overhead.
